<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theodosius I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 395 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theodosius I was a Roman emperor who died in 395 CE, the last to rule both the eastern and western halves of the empire. He made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicene-christianity">Nicene Christianity</a> the official religion of the state. After his death the empire was divided permanently between his sons, a division that accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> treat as a foundation of the eastern empire and accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> link to the west's decline.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/theodosius-i.jpg" alt="Theodosius I" width="270" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: www.livius.org · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bust_of_Theodosius_I.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
